# Project Structure

NestJS 11 + TypeORM + PostgreSQL API for BI binder parametrization.

## Root Layout

```
binder_parametrization/
├── src/                    # Application source (edit here)
├── dist/                   # Compiled output — do not edit
├── infra/postgres_data/    # Local Postgres volume (Docker)
├── .cursor/rules/          # Cursor agent rules
├── compose.yaml            # Dev stack: app + postgres_local
├── Dockerfile
├── .env.development        # Dev env vars (ConfigModule loads .env.${NODE_ENV})
├── nest-cli.json           # sourceRoot: src
├── package.json
├── tsconfig.json
└── tsconfig.build.json
```

## Entry Points

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/main.ts` | Bootstrap: Swagger (`/api`), CORS, cookie-parser, global ValidationPipe |
| `src/app.module.ts` | Root module — registers all feature modules |

## Feature Modules (`src/`)

Each active feature follows NestJS conventions: `*.module.ts`, `*.controller.ts`, `*.service.ts`, `*.entity.ts`.

| Folder | Status | Purpose |
|--------|--------|---------|
| `auth/` | Full module | JWT auth, global `AuthGuard`, decorators, roles |
| `user/` | Full module | User CRUD |
| `company/` | Full module | Company CRUD |
| `mail/` | Full module | Email via MailerSend |
| `database/` | Infrastructure | `TypeOrmModule.forRootAsync`, migrations, seeds |
| `parametrization/` | Entities only | `source.entity.ts`, `medium.entity.ts` |
| `ui-configuration/` | Entities only | `ui-platform`, `ui-channel`, `ui-buying-type` entities |
| `common/` | Shared | Cross-cutting enums (`role.enum.ts`, `source-type.enum.ts`) |

### Auth subfolders

- `auth/decorators/` — `@Public()`, `@Private()`, `@CurrentUser()`

### Database subfolders

- `database/migrations/` — TypeORM migrations (run via `npm run migration:run`)
- `database/seeds/` — Seed scripts (`npm run seed:run`)
- `database/typeorm.config.ts` — Shared TypeORM config (NestJS + CLI)
- `database/typeormFile.ts` — TypeORM CLI data source entry point

## Conventions

- **New features**: add a folder under `src/` with module/controller/service/entity, register entities via `TypeOrmModule.forFeature([...])`, then import in `app.module.ts`.
- **Entities without modules**: `parametrization/` and `ui-configuration/` hold TypeORM entities pending full modules — register via `TypeOrmModule.forFeature` in their future modules.
- **Env config**: `ConfigModule` is global; reads `./.env.${process.env.NODE_ENV}`.
- **Do not edit** `dist/`, `node_modules/`, or `infra/postgres_data/`.

## Useful Commands

```bash
npm run start:dev          # Dev server (port from APP_PORT, default 3000)
docker compose up          # App on :8090, Postgres on :55432
npm run migration:generate ./src/database/{migration_name} # Generate migration after entity changes
npm run migration:show #List migration status
npm run migration:run      # Apply migrations
npm run seed:run           # Run default seed
```
